,\n                                   8\n                                                                                            ORDER GRANTING CONDITIONAL\n                                                 v.                                         DISMISSAL\n                                   9\n\n                                  10     NISSAN NORTH AMERICA, INC.,\n                                                        Defendant.\n                                  11\n\n                                  12\nNorthern District of California\n United States District Court\n\n\n\n\n                                  13          The parties have advised that they have reached a settlement agreement. See Dkt. No. 23.\n\n                                  14   Accordingly, this case is DISMISSED WITH PREJUDICE and any dates and hearings are\n\n                                  15   VACATED; provided that, if any party certifies to this Court, with proper notice to opposing\n\n                                  16   counsel within sixty (60) days from the date below, that settlement has not in fact occurred, this\n\n                                  17   order shall be vacated and this cause shall be restored to the calendar for further proceedings.\n\n                                  18\n                                  19          IT IS SO ORDERED.\n\n                                  20   Dated: April 15, 2026\n\n                                  21\n\n                                  22\n                                                                                                    William H. Orrick\n                                  23                                                                United States District Judge\n                                  24\n\n                                  25\n\n                                  26\n                                  27\n\n                                  28\n\f", "ocr_status": 2, "date_upload": "2